00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.220
Just to get everyone up
to speed on what this is,

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.840
especially if this is your first time,

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.250
Khan Academy is a not
for profit with a mission

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.830
of providing a free world-class education

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.370
for anyone, anywhere.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:52.360
For many years we've
been building resources

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.530
for students both in the classroom

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:55.560
and outside of the classroom.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.970
Resources for teachers
inside the classroom.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:01.080
For parents so that they could learn

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:04.100
all the core or most of
the core academic skills

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.780
from starting with Pre-K
with Khan Academy Kids,

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.960
going into elementary level Mathematics,

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:09.950
English and Language Arts.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.600
We just launched some English
and Language Arts content

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.030
going into middle school then high school,

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.750
Math, Science, Humanities.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:19.060
And even things like free SAT practice

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.960
that we've partnered
with the college board.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:25.870
And when the school closure
situation became a reality,

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:29.720
we realized it's our duty
to step up even more.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.800
And so we've been trying to
create more and more supports

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.750
for teachers, parents, and students,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:36.910
to navigate this crisis.

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:40.450
Last week we released
things like daily schedules

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.220
for students of different ages.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.240
But think about how can you
put all of these resources

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.470
from Khan Academy and
resources from other players

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.620
together into a very coherent schedule

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.690
that can be something that bridges us

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.660
until schools reopen.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:56.380
We've been doing webinars
with teachers and parents

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.950
to get them up and running.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.920
And we've been doing this.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.220
This live stream which
we're calling a homeroom.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.410
