and college students.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.480
Especially when it comes to test taking.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:03:59.670
And so we wanted to help with that.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:00.980
But this is a great idea Sonya.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:04.020
I think we'd wanna do that.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.073
Let's see.

00:04:09.073 --> 00:04:12.950
We have Leo, says the
question, "In a unit test

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.670
or course challenge,
are they more difficult

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:16.240
than other questions?"

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:17.120
Good question, Leo.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.930
So today, the way Khan Academy works is,

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.470
when you do an exercise,

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:23.680
the exercise might ask
you to do five questions,

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.940
it's actually coming from a
pool of 20 or 30 questions.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.730
And so and whether
you're doing an exercise,

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:30.960
a unit test, or a quiz,

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.360
it's coming from various
pools of questions.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.690
When you're doing unit tests

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.480
you're doing multiple skills.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.080
So let's say a unit test
has 15 questions in,

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:42.610
or 10 questions in it,
it will then be sampling

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:45.170
from a pool of 300 questions.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.450
It is possible that you see questions

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:50.390
that you have seen in
the skill-focus practice

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.640
or the quizzes, or if you're
taking a core challenge,

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.100
in the unit task, but
it's unlikely, in fact,

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.830
it's very unlikely that you're
getting a complete repeats.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:00.680
And we've been doing a
lot of analytics on this.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.550
We think that the units
tasks and core challenge

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:03.930
are actually very indicative

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:05.950
of where you currently
are in your journey.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.460
We are exploring things like
making specialized unit tests

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:12.450
and core challenges that can
only be accessed in that way.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.890
But we're thinking
about whether that will,

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:16.770
whether that will actually

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:18.540
be significantly better
than what is there,

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.220
but that's the current
thing that you have.

