00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.680
- Question, Sal, from Mathematics C,

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.127
and this is really important one.

00:07:21.127 --> 00:07:23.777
"Why are getting questions
wrong so important?"

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:28.020
- So, getting questions
wrong, and obviously,

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:29.157
you don't wanna get a question wrong

00:07:29.157 --> 00:07:30.560
if you can get it right,

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.620
it's not like that's
gonna do you any good.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.380
But, a lot of times when
you do anything in life,

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:40.270
whether it's math or
free throws, anything,

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:44.360
when you fail, we oftentimes
kind of beat up on ourselves,

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.500
sometimes get discouraged,

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.720
it hits our ego a little bit, our pride.

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.240
I'm like, aw, maybe I don't
need to do this thing,

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:51.910
and you're oftentimes
tempted to disengage.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:54.913
And the thing to remember is,

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:59.370
that those times that you've failed,

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.570
you're kind of discovering your edge.

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:03.370
And it's when you operate in your edge

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.630
that you're going to grow the most.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.590
And so there's even been research studies

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:10.590
that when people fail at something,

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:13.660
let's say a cognitive
task like a math question,

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:18.550
but then they reflect why they
failed, why they got it wrong

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:20.240
and how they could've done it differently,

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:22.230
that's actually when you form (mumbles).

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.520
Those of you who are familiar with things

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.870
like weightlifting oftentimes
you'll hear people say,

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:29.100
oh, you should do some reps until failure.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:30.140
Failure is a good thing,

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:32.720
it shows that you've had a real workout.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:34.840
Sometimes failure has been stigmatized

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:37.150
because you're like, oh, if I fail a test,

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:40.100
that's bad, I got an F,
or if I got a bad grade,

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:41.350
or if I get questions on a test,

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:43.200
and then it reflects on me.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.740
And that's why at Khan Academy,

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:47.560
I just described how
our items are created.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.840
We wanna give you as
many chances as possible

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:54.220
to show that you can become
proficient in a concept.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:56.490
And so, it's not that when you do it once,

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:59.130
you got 80%, you got 20% wrong,

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:02.260
all of a sudden you're just
labeled 80% student forever.

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:03.730
You can keep going at it.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.850
This idea generally speaking
is called mastery learning,

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.830
it predates Khan Academy.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.500
Many advocacy studies showing

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.840
that it can accelerate folks' learning.

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:13.690
It was just hard to
implement, historically,

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:15.680
if you didn't have some tools

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.080
that can have almost an infinite number

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:20.080
of questions give you immediate feedback,

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.540
and be able to personalize
the individual student's pace.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:27.080
But that's why failure,
when you fail on a question

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.290
that you can kind of engage
in, you should reflect.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.900
That's when your brain growing the most,

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.810
and you just have to reflect
on why you got it wrong.

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:34.550
And then you're gonna, you're gonna

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.200
your growth will only accelerate.

